==Strategy==
Given that the only non-[[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy here is Project A, you can omit units that target specifically [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] from your loadout as they will do little throughout the stage. Still, it's best to bring a [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Warp immune]] meatshield such as [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] to prevent a stray Warp from obliterating your frontline. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] works great here, as it can use the Dogensteins as stepping stones to deal chip damage to the backliners. Alternatively, tankers such as [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] or [[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]] work very well to hold off enemies and also deal chip damage to the main threats.

The most effective way to go about this stage is to wait for the enemies to clump up, then freeze them with [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]] before hitting them with an [[Explosion]] talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Usually this will be enough to take out the Project A, Camelle, and Rain D provided you keep meatshielding, after which Master A. will be the only main enemy left to clean up.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST Exclusives]]: Most of these will do well on this stage. If needed use the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt Cannon]] to ensure they get at least a few good hits in. Notably, anything that can snipe Camelle will be especially useful.

==Trivia==
*Small Inlet, Large Field's Japanese name, Ōkusabara no Chīsana Irie, (大草原の小さな入り江 , "Little Inlet on the Pairie"), is a play on ''Ōkusabara no Chīsana Ie'' (大草原の小さな家, "''[[wikipedia:Little House on the Prairie|Little House on the Prairie]]''").

